{"kind":"assert","text":"Operator direction, hugh, 2026-08-30, revising the web reputation discussion: domain-level reputation is not granular enough for useful checks, so individual URLs are tracked. The assessing agent additionally provides OTEL-flavored reputation reports directly from Safe Browsing or VirusTotal - an example companion script is provided for it to call - and those reports maintain the materialized data consistently over time, removing the need for a side-cache of checked URLs. There is no spoofability, authority, or trust boundary of interest: all OTLP sources are local, and a harness log carrying a URL is not significantly distinct from an agent script sending a url-reputation record - an accepted shape of this application under the locally-deployed target model. Actual URLs, the exclusion list, and the reputation feed are all OTLP-flavored inputs to the same pipeline. The resulting loopback pipeline, the most complex yet, deliberately demonstrates that Tailapp inputs need not be agent-harness instrumentation."}